---
title: Stuart rotates a key with a Singleton Beacon, Satoshi verifies
---

%% Use case: Stuart and Satoshi are peers in a p2p, Signal-like messaging channel.
%% Each peer is identified by a did:btcr2 DID. Satoshi trusts Stuart's keys at version N.

sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor Stu as Stuart (DID controller)
    participant BTC as Bitcoin blockchain ⛓
    participant CAS as CAS / IPFS 📦 (optional)
    actor Sat as Satoshi (channel peer)
    participant Res as Satoshi's resolver

    Note over Stu,Res: Before: the channel uses Stuart's key at version N. Satoshi trusts this key.

    rect rgba(128, 128, 128, 0.08)
    Note over Stu: 1. Construct the update
    Stu->>Stu: Resolve own DID (minConf 6) → versionId N
    Stu->>Stu: Patch: add the new key to verificationMethod,<br/>make it the authentication and capabilityInvocation key,<br/>replace the Singleton Beacons of the old key with one for the new key
    Stu->>Stu: Construct the BTCR2 Unsigned Update (targetVersionId N + 1)
    Stu->>Stu: Sign with the current capabilityInvocation key<br/>(Data Integrity Proof, bip340-jcs-2025), then verify the proof
    end

    rect rgba(128, 128, 128, 0.08)
    Note over Stu,BTC: 2. Announce through the Singleton Beacon
    Stu->>Stu: Signal Bytes = SHA256(JCS(BTCR2 Signed Update))
    Note over Stu,BTC: The Beacon Address must hold a UTXO (funded at setup).<br/>Send the change to the new Beacon Address for the next Beacon Signal.
    Stu->>Stu: Build the Beacon Signal: spend a UTXO of the Beacon Address,<br/>last output OP_RETURN Signal Bytes. Sign with the Beacon Address key.
    Stu->>BTC: Broadcast the Beacon Signal
    BTC-->>Stu: minConf (6) confirmations
    Note over Stu: Do not start the next update before this point.
    end

    rect rgba(128, 128, 128, 0.08)
    Note over Stu,Sat: 3. Distribute the update data
    alt CAS distribution (public)
        Stu->>CAS: Publish the BTCR2 Signed Update (under its hash)
    else Sidecar distribution (private)
        Stu->>Stu: Keep the BTCR2 Signed Update for the life of the DID
    end
    Stu->>Sat: Channel message signed with the new key,<br/>did and Sidecar Data (all updates, if Sidecar distribution)
    end

    rect rgba(128, 128, 128, 0.08)
    Note over Sat,Res: 4. Satoshi verifies
    Sat->>Sat: Message key is not a trusted key → resolve
    Sat->>Res: resolve(did, { sidecar })
    Res->>Res: Establish current_document (version 1)
    Res->>BTC: Find Beacon Signals of each Beacon Address
    BTC-->>Res: Beacon Signal (Signal Bytes = update_hash), block metadata
    alt Update in the Sidecar Data
        Res->>Res: Get the update from update_lookup_table
    else Update not in the Sidecar Data
        Res->>CAS: Get the document by update_hash
        CAS-->>Res: BTCR2 Signed Update (hash checked)
    end
    Res->>Res: Process Next Update: check sourceHash, targetVersionId,<br/>proof, and targetHash, then apply the patch
    Res-->>Sat: didDocument (version N + 1) and didDocumentMetadata
    Sat->>Sat: Check: not deactivated, versionId ≥ N,<br/>new key is in authentication
    Sat->>Sat: Verify the channel message with the new key.<br/>Trust the new key. Stop trusting the old key.
    end
